WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:00:01.150 --> 00:00:03.650
Wealth, fame, power...

3
00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:04.440
Gold Roger, the King of the Pirates,

4
00:00:03.650 --> 00:00:07.820
Gold Roger, the King of the Pirates, obtained everything the world has to offer.

5
00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:07.360
attained this and everything else
the world had to offer.

6
00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:10.820
And his dying words drove
countless souls to the seas.

7
00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:11.660
What he said in his final moments drove countless souls to the seas.

8
00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:13.660
You want my treasure?

9
00:00:12.370 --> 00:00:13.700
You can have it!

10
00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:15.450
Go ahead.

11
00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:17.040
I left everything I gathered
together in one place.

12
00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:16.660
Find it!

13
00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:19.250
Everything is right where I left it!

14
00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:19.250
Now you just have to find it!

15
00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:23.750
These words lured
men to the Grand Line

16
00:00:21.670 --> 00:00:26.380
People set their sights on the Grand Line in pursuit of their dreams.

17
00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:26.920
in pursuit of dreams greater than
they'd ever dared to imagine!

18
00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:29.630
The world has truly entered the Great Pirate Era!

19
00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:29.850
This is the time known as
the Great Pirate Era!

20
00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:35.640
Come aboard and bring along all your hopes and dreams

21
00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:41.440
I know together we'll find everything we're looking for

22
00:00:41.770 --> 00:00:42.690
One Piece!

23
00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:52.700
Compasses? Not for me. Left them all behind

24
00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:58.500
I'm headed out to sea, with my heart serving as guide

25
00:00:59.330 --> 00:01:04.540
Following the ancient map to the spot marked "X" reveals

26
00:01:04.540 --> 00:01:09.760
Yeah, it's only legendary till someone proves it's real

27
00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:13.710
When the world's got you down,

28
00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:16.850
lean on your crew, they'll turn it around

29
00:01:17.180 --> 00:01:22.190
Their biorhythm will carry you through

30
00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:24.230
We're gonna make the most of it

31
00:01:26.110 --> 00:01:31.400
Come aboard and bring along all your hopes and dreams

32
00:01:31.610 --> 00:01:36.990
I know together we'll find everything we're looking for

33
00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:40.040
Got some change to my name,

34
00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:43.250
and maybe you wanna be my friend?

35
00:01:43.540 --> 00:01:48.130
We are, we are on the cruise!

36
00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:49.760
WE ARE!

37
00:01:50.010 --> 00:01:56.260
<b>Captain Kuro</b>

38
00:01:52.510 --> 00:01:54.510
[KLAHADORE] Don't call
it murder, Jango.

39
00:01:54.510 --> 00:01:56.300
I don't like the sound of it.

40
00:01:56.300 --> 00:01:58.140
[JANGO] Oh, right, accident.

41
00:01:58.140 --> 00:01:59.770
It's an accident...
that you planned.

42
00:02:01.850 --> 00:02:04.150
Uh, what are those guys
talking about?

43
00:02:04.150 --> 00:02:05.900
Just be quiet.

44
00:02:05.900 --> 00:02:08.570
Maybe if we listen
a little closer, we can find out.

45
00:02:08.570 --> 00:02:10.490
[KLAHADORE] We
can't simply kill her.

46
00:02:10.490 --> 00:02:14.820
It is critical to our plan that
Miss Kaya perishes in an unfortunate accident.

47
00:02:14.820 --> 00:02:17.030
So don't screw that up!

48
00:02:17.780 --> 00:02:20.910
So basically, on your signal,
the men and I storm the village

49
00:02:20.910 --> 00:02:24.460
and manage to "accidentally" kill
the little rich girl.

50
00:02:24.460 --> 00:02:27.710
Then you get her inheritance
and we all get paid, right?

51
00:02:27.710 --> 00:02:28.670
You moron!

52
00:02:28.670 --> 00:02:30.590
Your ignorance is astounding!

53
00:02:30.590 --> 00:02:34.130
We're not related, so how
could I inherit anything from her?

54
00:02:34.130 --> 00:02:36.010
[JANGO] You'll work
very hard to!

55
00:02:36.010 --> 00:02:38.600
[KLAHADORE]
No Jango, I won't.

56
00:02:38.600 --> 00:02:41.640
Now listen to me, this is
the most important part.

57
00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:46.060
Before you kill her, you'll use your
hypnosis to make Kaya write her will.

58
00:02:46.060 --> 00:02:50.530
And it will say, "I leave my entire
fortune to my butler, Klahadore".

59
00:02:50.530 --> 00:02:51.480
[USOPP gasps]

60
00:02:52.440 --> 00:02:57.450
Then, and only then, will I have
undisputed control of her enormous fortune.

61
00:02:57.450 --> 00:03:00.910
And no one will
suspect a thing.

62
00:03:00.910 --> 00:03:01.790
[USOPP whimpers]

63
00:03:01.790 --> 00:03:05.750
[KLAHADORE] I have spent three long years
gaining the trust of everyone around me

64
00:03:05.750 --> 00:03:07.540
so that it would be
unsurprising for her

65
00:03:07.540 --> 00:03:11.460
to leave the entirety
of her inheritance to me.

66
00:03:11.460 --> 00:03:14.800
[JANGO] Three years
as a butler for this, huh?

67
00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:19.390
You sure had us scared
back then, Captain Kuro.

68
00:03:19.390 --> 00:03:23.930
Three years ago, you suddenly said
you were giving up life as a pirate.

69
00:03:23.930 --> 00:03:27.190
In no time at all you set up
someone to be your double.

70
00:03:27.190 --> 00:03:30.860
Then you let the world see
Captain Kuro get executed.

71
00:03:41.450 --> 00:03:45.330
Only now, do I understand that was
just the beginning of this plan.

72
00:03:45.330 --> 00:03:47.370
You are the "Man
of a Thousand Plans."

73
00:03:47.370 --> 00:03:51.880
Never call me that again.
I abandoned that name years ago.

74
00:03:51.880 --> 00:03:56.630
I now wish to obtain my wealth without attracting
the attention of the government.

75
00:03:56.630 --> 00:03:58.760
In other words, I'm a pacifist.

76
00:03:58.760 --> 00:04:02.810
[laughing] Some pacifist you are!

77
00:04:02.810 --> 00:04:08.190
Murdering an entire family
doesn't exactly qualify as peaceful.

78
00:04:08.190 --> 00:04:11.730
Hold on, I haven't murdered
an entire family.

79
00:04:11.730 --> 00:04:13.570
The father's death
wasn't planned.

80
00:04:13.570 --> 00:04:16.070
[JANGO] Whatever you say,
it makes no difference to me.

81
00:04:16.070 --> 00:04:19.030
If it's all the same to you,
hurry up and give the word.

82
00:04:19.030 --> 00:04:20.910
The crew is getting bored.

83
00:04:20.910 --> 00:04:24.080
We've been waiting in the waters
near here for over a week,

84
00:04:24.660 --> 00:04:27.710
and the men are growing
more anxious by the minute.

85
00:04:33.880 --> 00:04:35.460
[USOPP] This is horrible!
This is really horrible!

86
00:04:37.550 --> 00:04:40.050
[USOPP grunting]

87
00:04:40.050 --> 00:04:41.680
What are they talking about?

88
00:04:41.680 --> 00:04:43.050
Is it bad guy stuff?

89
00:04:43.050 --> 00:04:46.600
What? Weren't you listening
to any of that?

90
00:04:46.600 --> 00:04:47.930
Those guys aren't just
bad, they're evil!

91
00:04:47.930 --> 00:04:52.020
Captain Kuro is known to be the most
devious, scheming pirate around!

92
00:04:52.020 --> 00:04:55.980
And though he's known for his smarts,
he's legendary for his brutality.

93
00:04:55.980 --> 00:05:00.240
Word had it that the Marines caught
and executed him three years ago,

94
00:05:00.240 --> 00:05:05.200
but Captain Kuro is alive and well,
posing as Klahadore the butler!

95
00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:10.830
And he's had his diabolical sights set on
Kaya's fortune for the last three years!

96
00:05:11.870 --> 00:05:15.550
[USOPP] First, they'll attack
the village, then they'll kill Kaya!

97
00:05:15.550 --> 00:05:17.210
[KAYA whimpers]

98
00:05:20.590 --> 00:05:22.890
[USOPP] This is bad!
This is seriously bad!

99
00:05:25.680 --> 00:05:27.970
Hey, get down!
They'll see you!

100
00:05:27.970 --> 00:05:31.190
Hey, bad guys! You better
stay away from that girl!

101
00:05:31.190 --> 00:05:33.230
[USOPP groans]

102
00:05:33.230 --> 00:05:34.400
[JANGO] Who are you?!

103
00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:37.320
You idiot,
they've spotted you!

104
00:05:37.320 --> 00:05:39.360
Come on! Hurry up and hide before they
decide you need a long slow death!

105
00:05:40.990 --> 00:05:43.740
Well now, if it isn't Usopp,
the mischievous town liar.

106
00:05:44.990 --> 00:05:46.700
[screams] Oh, no!
I'm spotted too!

107
00:05:47.330 --> 00:05:50.620
[KURO] Did you...
hear anything?

108
00:05:50.620 --> 00:05:52.960
Uh, nope. Nothing at all.
I don't know what you mean.

109
00:05:52.960 --> 00:05:54.630
We didn't hear a peep.
We just got here,

110
00:05:54.630 --> 00:05:56.380
so we didn't hear
anything about anything!

111
00:05:56.380 --> 00:05:57.300
We heard it all!

112
00:05:57.300 --> 00:05:59.550
Shut up!

113
00:05:59.550 --> 00:06:01.470
[KURO chuckles]

114
00:06:03.760 --> 00:06:05.720
[JANGO] Well, if you say so.

115
00:06:08.180 --> 00:06:09.560
[JANGO] Pay attention, boys!

116
00:06:09.560 --> 00:06:11.730
And watch this ring closely.

117
00:06:12.440 --> 00:06:14.310
[LUFFY] Hm? Okay.

118
00:06:14.310 --> 00:06:17.440
Don't you get it? It's
some kind of weapon, we gotta run!

119
00:06:18.440 --> 00:06:21.690
[JANGO] By the count of "Jango,"
you will be in a deep sleep.

120
00:06:21.690 --> 00:06:23.150
Are you ready?

121
00:06:23.150 --> 00:06:24.530
One... Two...

122
00:06:23.150 --> 00:06:26.120
[USOPP] Run for cover!
He's gonna kill us!

123
00:06:26.120 --> 00:06:27.070
[JANGO] Jango!

124
00:06:27.410 --> 00:06:31.040
– [USOPP whimpers] Heh?
– [LUFFY snores]

125
00:06:31.040 --> 00:06:33.830
– [JANGO snoring]
– Jango, you idiot!

126
00:06:33.830 --> 00:06:36.040
I see you're still falling
asleep on the job!

127
00:06:37.630 --> 00:06:39.380
– [LUFFY snoring]
– [USOPP] Hey, be careful!

128
00:06:39.380 --> 00:06:40.880
You're gonna fall!

129
00:06:42.760 --> 00:06:44.680
[USOPP whimpers]

130
00:06:44.680 --> 00:06:47.800
He had to go and fall
off a cliff, didn't he?

131
00:06:47.800 --> 00:06:52.930
A pity really, I didn't mean to kill him,
but there's no way he could've survived.

132
00:06:52.930 --> 00:06:55.770
[USOPP] This can't
be happening!

133
00:06:55.770 --> 00:06:57.020
They killed him!

134
00:06:57.020 --> 00:06:59.940
He's really... dead!

135
00:06:59.940 --> 00:07:01.480
[JANGO] What
about the other one?

136
00:07:01.480 --> 00:07:03.240
Shall I take care of him?

137
00:07:03.240 --> 00:07:04.820
There's no need.

138
00:07:04.820 --> 00:07:07.620
Everything he could say
would sound like, lies.

139
00:07:06.660 --> 00:07:08.570
[USOPP gasps]

140
00:07:09.580 --> 00:07:11.620
[KURO] Jango,
tomorrow at daybreak,

141
00:07:11.620 --> 00:07:13.960
the men are
to attack the village.

142
00:07:13.960 --> 00:07:16.170
Rough up the villagers some and tear up
their homes a little, for good measure.

143
00:07:16.170 --> 00:07:20.540
And above all, make sure
Miss Kaya's death looks accidental.

144
00:07:22.210 --> 00:07:23.340
Tomorrow...

145
00:07:23.340 --> 00:07:27.840
Just accept it, Usopp. There
is nothing you can say or do

146
00:07:27.840 --> 00:07:30.510
to warn the villagers
of this impending tragedy.

147
00:07:30.510 --> 00:07:34.980
[USOPP gasps, screams]

148
00:07:35.890 --> 00:07:37.350
[JANGO] Are you sure
about that one?

149
00:07:37.350 --> 00:07:40.400
[KURO] Of course I am,
my plans are flawless.

150
00:07:45.360 --> 00:07:46.450
[USOPP] I can't believe this!

151
00:07:46.450 --> 00:07:49.910
This is terrible!
I gotta do something!

152
00:07:49.910 --> 00:07:54.910
Everyone in the village I grew up with is
in danger, and Kaya's gonna be killed!

153
00:07:57.870 --> 00:07:58.870
[KAYA] Who are you?

154
00:07:58.870 --> 00:08:02.340
[USOPP] I'm Usopp,
brave warrior of the sea!

155
00:08:02.340 --> 00:08:05.130
[USOPP laughs] I heard you've
been a little down lately,

156
00:08:05.130 --> 00:08:08.010
so I thought I'd tell you
a story to cheer you up!

157
00:08:08.010 --> 00:08:09.890
[KAYA] You would do well
to mind your own business!

158
00:08:10.890 --> 00:08:12.640
Please leave or I'll call
someone who will make you leave!

159
00:08:13.220 --> 00:08:18.560
[KAYA laughs] And then?
What happened after that?

160
00:08:18.560 --> 00:08:20.310
[USOPP] I fought, of course!

161
00:08:32.410 --> 00:08:33.410
Hold on.

162
00:08:33.410 --> 00:08:35.830
I thought Luffy was supposed
to be with him.

163
00:08:37.750 --> 00:08:38.790
[ALL] Captain!

164
00:08:38.790 --> 00:08:40.330
[ALL yelp]

165
00:08:40.330 --> 00:08:42.670
Hey, where's Luffy?
Is he still at the shore?

166
00:08:46.760 --> 00:08:48.800
Wow, he looked really upset.

167
00:08:48.800 --> 00:08:51.340
But why? Still mad
at the butler?

168
00:08:52.390 --> 00:08:54.100
[ZORO] Who knows.

169
00:08:54.100 --> 00:08:56.810
No! That wasn't
just a mad face!

170
00:08:56.810 --> 00:08:58.230
That look was different!

171
00:08:58.230 --> 00:09:01.850
It was the tragic face
of sheer desperation!

172
00:09:01.850 --> 00:09:03.060
Hey.

173
00:09:03.060 --> 00:09:04.820
Why don't you guys show us the way
to get down to that shore.

174
00:09:04.820 --> 00:09:06.900
[CARROT] This smells
like an adventure to me!

175
00:09:06.900 --> 00:09:09.200
Yeah! Something happened
at the shore!

176
00:09:09.200 --> 00:09:11.360
[ONION] I think this calls
for the Usopp Pirates!

177
00:09:11.360 --> 00:09:14.240
Enough already!
How do we get to this place?!

178
00:09:15.790 --> 00:09:17.450
[USOPP] Terrible news.

179
00:09:19.080 --> 00:09:23.580
Pirates! Pirates are coming!
Everybody run!

180
00:09:23.580 --> 00:09:27.960
We don't stand a chance!
Everybody run! Run!

181
00:09:30.130 --> 00:09:33.720
[USOPP] Tomorrow morning they're gonna
attack the village, we gotta get outta here!

182
00:09:33.720 --> 00:09:35.760
What're you doing?! Run!

183
00:09:53.490 --> 00:09:54.700
[VILLAGER D] Alright, Usopp.

184
00:09:54.700 --> 00:09:56.200
Enough is enough.

185
00:09:56.200 --> 00:09:57.200
[VILLAGER E] We
can't take it anymore.

186
00:09:57.200 --> 00:09:59.200
We're putting a stop
to this here and now.

187
00:09:59.200 --> 00:10:00.200
It's for your own good.

188
00:10:00.200 --> 00:10:01.870
[USOPP] No! It's not like that!

189
00:10:02.620 --> 00:10:03.960
It's the truth
this time! I promise!

190
00:10:03.960 --> 00:10:07.290
Stop it! We all know
that you're nothing but a liar.

191
00:10:07.290 --> 00:10:11.840
It would do you some good to follow
Klahadore's example of hard work and honesty.

192
00:10:12.550 --> 00:10:15.970
[KURO] Everything he could
say would sound like lies.

193
00:10:18.680 --> 00:10:19.640
[USOPP] Oh no.

194
00:10:19.640 --> 00:10:22.230
This is exactly what
Klahadore's counting on.

195
00:10:22.230 --> 00:10:25.520
He ignored me because he knew
no one would believe me.

196
00:10:31.860 --> 00:10:34.110
[MERRY] Are these to your liking, miss?

197
00:10:34.740 --> 00:10:38.490
[MERRY] Custom made
to your exact specifications.

198
00:10:38.490 --> 00:10:40.700
It was quite a trip
to get them.

199
00:10:40.700 --> 00:10:42.580
[KAYA] They're just perfect.

200
00:10:43.580 --> 00:10:47.130
Thank you so much for traveling
so far to get them for me.

201
00:10:53.760 --> 00:10:55.300
They're a gift aren't they?

202
00:10:55.300 --> 00:10:56.550
Yes.

203
00:10:56.550 --> 00:10:58.890
As of tomorrow, it will be
exactly three years to the day

204
00:10:58.890 --> 00:11:01.060
since Klahadore arrived here.

205
00:11:01.060 --> 00:11:03.310
He's always taken
such good care of me.

206
00:11:03.850 --> 00:11:06.480
[MERRY] He'll be delighted
to receive such a lovely gift.

207
00:11:06.480 --> 00:11:08.020
[KAYA] I hope so.

208
00:11:10.020 --> 00:11:12.900
Please hear me out, everyone!
Our lives depend on it!

209
00:11:12.900 --> 00:11:13.900
Listen!

210
00:11:13.900 --> 00:11:15.610
Pirates are gonna attack
the village in the morning!

211
00:11:15.610 --> 00:11:17.870
If we believed every story
you ever told us,

212
00:11:17.870 --> 00:11:20.990
we would've run screaming from
the village hundreds a times already.

213
00:11:20.990 --> 00:11:23.580
[USOPP] Please, believe me!
We don't have time!

214
00:11:23.580 --> 00:11:26.710
I'm not lying
this time. I swear!

215
00:11:26.710 --> 00:11:29.500
Don't you get it?!
They'll murder you all!

216
00:11:29.500 --> 00:11:32.210
[VILLAGER E] You'll be lucky
if we don't murder you!

217
00:11:35.630 --> 00:11:37.760
[USOPP] I'm not lying!

218
00:11:37.760 --> 00:11:40.050
[VILLAGER E] Get him!
Don't let him escape!

219
00:11:47.940 --> 00:11:54.400
[KURO] After three long years of absence,
I made the call for my men, and you came.

220
00:11:54.400 --> 00:11:57.570
Your loyalty
will be richly rewarded.

221
00:11:57.570 --> 00:12:01.490
I intend on being more than generous
when I divide the take.

222
00:12:01.490 --> 00:12:05.580
At dawn tomorrow, destroy the village
to your hearts content.

223
00:12:05.580 --> 00:12:09.500
[PIRATES yelling, cheering]

224
00:12:12.800 --> 00:12:13.920
[KIDS] What?!

225
00:12:13.920 --> 00:12:16.170
Pirates are going
to attack the village?!

226
00:12:16.170 --> 00:12:19.470
Then they're gonna kill Kaya?!

227
00:12:20.340 --> 00:12:22.680
Yep. That's what they said.
No question 'bout it.

228
00:12:21.970 --> 00:12:24.470
[ALL yelping]

229
00:12:25.520 --> 00:12:30.190
So, what made you think
it'd be a good time for a nap?

230
00:12:30.190 --> 00:12:35.190
That's the thing, I don't remember going
to sleep or getting down here at all!

231
00:12:35.190 --> 00:12:37.320
This proves it!
Klahadore is a bad guy!

232
00:12:37.320 --> 00:12:39.070
Usopp saw right through him!

233
00:12:39.070 --> 00:12:42.990
I bet he's on his way to warn the villagers
so they'll have time to run away.

234
00:12:42.990 --> 00:12:44.080
Well, that's perfect.

235
00:12:44.080 --> 00:12:47.450
Those stupid pirates won't hurt anyone
because the town will be abandoned

236
00:12:47.450 --> 00:12:49.000
by the time they get there!

237
00:12:49.000 --> 00:12:49.960
Yeah, that's right!

238
00:12:49.960 --> 00:12:52.130
We'd better run away
too if we wanna live!

239
00:12:52.130 --> 00:12:53.670
[PEPPER] Alright, let's pack
our treasure and...

240
00:12:53.670 --> 00:12:55.960
[KIDS] Run like the wind! Ah!

241
00:12:57.920 --> 00:12:58.880
Oh no!

242
00:12:58.880 --> 00:12:59.720
What's up?

243
00:12:59.720 --> 00:13:00.630
[LUFFY screaming]

244
00:13:00.630 --> 00:13:03.850
We need to stock up
before the meat shop guy leaves!

245
00:13:04.970 --> 00:13:07.180
[ZORO] C'mon, that's not
really the issue at hand here.

246
00:13:24.240 --> 00:13:25.070
Usopp.

247
00:13:32.830 --> 00:13:35.340
Oh, good. I was worried
you wouldn't come back.

248
00:13:36.500 --> 00:13:38.340
Quick! Run, Kaya!

249
00:13:38.340 --> 00:13:39.550
They're gonna kill you!

250
00:13:39.550 --> 00:13:41.180
Huh?

251
00:13:41.180 --> 00:13:42.630
Someone's going to kill me?

252
00:13:42.630 --> 00:13:44.550
He's tricked the entire village!

253
00:13:44.550 --> 00:13:46.720
Klahadore's really a
deadly pirate captain!

254
00:13:47.720 --> 00:13:50.480
Is this a story?

255
00:13:50.480 --> 00:13:52.270
Well, I don't like this one.

256
00:13:52.270 --> 00:13:53.560
[USOPP] Uh.

257
00:13:53.560 --> 00:13:55.190
This isn't one of my stories!

258
00:13:55.190 --> 00:13:57.480
It's the truth! I heard
it with my own ears!

259
00:13:59.150 --> 00:14:02.240
[USOPP] Klahadore is a pirate captain who
weaseled his way into your family's home

260
00:14:02.240 --> 00:14:03.700
so he could steal
your fortune.

261
00:14:03.700 --> 00:14:05.570
He's pretended to be
your butler for three years

262
00:14:05.570 --> 00:14:07.910
so he can kill you
and inherit your money!

263
00:14:07.910 --> 00:14:11.160
[KAYA] What are
you talking about, Usopp?

264
00:14:11.160 --> 00:14:13.330
His crew is gonna raid
the village at dawn

265
00:14:13.330 --> 00:14:16.130
and in the process,
you're gonna get killed!

266
00:14:20.460 --> 00:14:23.720
Klahadore is a very bad man,
your life is in danger!

267
00:14:23.720 --> 00:14:25.590
You have to escape!

268
00:14:26.600 --> 00:14:28.510
[KAYA] He did treat
you harshly earlier

269
00:14:28.510 --> 00:14:34.690
and I understand that you're hurt,
but lying like this, it's not like you.

270
00:14:36.310 --> 00:14:39.110
Kaya, please.
I'm telling you the truth.

271
00:14:41.490 --> 00:14:44.150
I loved them.

272
00:14:44.150 --> 00:14:45.950
Every... one.

273
00:14:48.370 --> 00:14:52.120
All those lies you told me.
They brought joy to my heart.

274
00:14:52.120 --> 00:14:55.330
But... this is
just vengeful poison.

275
00:14:57.040 --> 00:14:58.290
Kaya, please.

276
00:14:58.290 --> 00:15:01.460
Listen to me, I'm not just trying
to get back at Klahadore.

277
00:15:01.460 --> 00:15:05.010
Why would you do that?
It's wrong.

278
00:15:05.010 --> 00:15:06.390
Kaya... I...

279
00:15:06.390 --> 00:15:07.760
[USOPP, KAYA laughing]

280
00:15:07.760 --> 00:15:10.510
Miss Kaya, is
everything okay up here?

281
00:15:10.510 --> 00:15:12.560
[gasps]

282
00:15:15.560 --> 00:15:16.800
Let's get out of here!

283
00:15:16.880 --> 00:15:17.710
Right now!

284
00:15:20.070 --> 00:15:21.730
[USOPP grunts]

285
00:15:23.360 --> 00:15:24.110
of this village

286
00:15:24.110 --> 00:15:24.900
Let's get out of

287
00:15:25.650 --> 00:15:28.200
before that butler gets back.

288
00:15:40.420 --> 00:15:41.590
Stop it!

289
00:15:44.720 --> 00:15:45.260
[USOPP] C'mon!

290
00:15:50.680 --> 00:15:54.680
I promise this'll all make sense
tomorrow, but right now we need to go.

291
00:15:54.680 --> 00:15:55.560
Kaya, please.

292
00:15:55.560 --> 00:15:57.440
– Please... Trust me.
– [KAYA gasps]

293
00:15:57.440 --> 00:15:58.690
[slap]

294
00:16:05.240 --> 00:16:06.900
You're pathetic.

295
00:16:17.960 --> 00:16:20.290
Leave Miss Kaya alone,
you maniac!

296
00:16:23.670 --> 00:16:24.800
No!

297
00:16:24.800 --> 00:16:26.090
[USOPP grunts]

298
00:16:26.090 --> 00:16:27.300
[gasps]

299
00:16:36.270 --> 00:16:37.640
[VILLAGERS yelling]

300
00:16:37.640 --> 00:16:39.270
Don't let that lunatic get away!

301
00:16:39.270 --> 00:16:42.190
He broke in and tried
to kidnap the lady of the house!

302
00:16:42.190 --> 00:16:47.570
[VILLAGERS yelling]

303
00:16:49.150 --> 00:16:50.660
[USOPP] Why?

304
00:16:51.820 --> 00:16:53.830
Why won't
anyone believe me?

305
00:16:57.000 --> 00:17:01.170
[VILLAGERS yelling]

306
00:17:06.090 --> 00:17:07.970
Usopp...

307
00:17:09.130 --> 00:17:11.680
There, there, ma'am,
everything's going to be fine.

308
00:17:28.440 --> 00:17:30.450
[KIDS] Captain!

309
00:17:33.030 --> 00:17:34.620
Hey! How's it going, guys?

310
00:17:34.620 --> 00:17:37.160
– [CARROT] Hey, Captain!
– [PEPPER] Look, he's back!

311
00:17:38.160 --> 00:17:40.120
Wait! You're alive again?!

312
00:17:40.120 --> 00:17:41.500
Alive?

313
00:17:41.500 --> 00:17:43.670
Yeah! And I had
a pretty good nap!

314
00:17:43.670 --> 00:17:45.380
He was sleeping
the whole time!

315
00:17:45.380 --> 00:17:48.510
Captain, we heard all about those
pirates and their evil plan!

316
00:17:48.510 --> 00:17:52.550
We'd better hurry and warn the people
in the village so they have time to get away!

317
00:17:52.550 --> 00:17:54.010
Warn the people...

318
00:17:57.010 --> 00:17:58.470
You're pathetic.

319
00:18:00.930 --> 00:18:01.810
Stop it.

320
00:18:01.810 --> 00:18:03.900
We all know you're
nothing but a liar.

321
00:18:12.610 --> 00:18:15.070
Well, obviously,
I'm lying like usual!

322
00:18:15.070 --> 00:18:17.080
That butler made
me so mad with what he said,

323
00:18:17.080 --> 00:18:20.040
I thought I'd get him back
and say that he was a pirate!

324
00:18:20.040 --> 00:18:21.710
[KIDS, USOPP laughing]

325
00:18:21.710 --> 00:18:22.620
[ONION] Oh, I get it!

326
00:18:22.620 --> 00:18:24.880
You put the straw hat
guy up to it, too!

327
00:18:24.880 --> 00:18:30.340
[ALL laughing]

328
00:18:30.340 --> 00:18:32.720
Hey. Where ya goin'?

329
00:18:32.720 --> 00:18:35.720
[CARROT] Honestly,
you've really disappointed me.

330
00:18:35.720 --> 00:18:36.470
Yeah.

331
00:18:36.470 --> 00:18:38.180
Even though that butler guy is a jerk,

332
00:18:38.180 --> 00:18:40.560
I thought you were better
than lying to hurt someone,

333
00:18:40.560 --> 00:18:44.140
and I admired you for being
such a kind-hearted person.

334
00:18:44.140 --> 00:18:47.440
[ONION] And to think, we
respected you this entire time.

335
00:18:47.440 --> 00:18:48.320
[CARROT] Let's go home.

336
00:18:48.320 --> 00:18:50.030
[PEPPER] Yeah,
it's suppertime anyways.

337
00:18:50.030 --> 00:18:51.570
[ONION] Wonder
what we're having.

338
00:18:57.370 --> 00:18:59.910
So, how come
you lied to them?

339
00:18:59.910 --> 00:19:02.370
Because all I do is lie.

340
00:19:02.370 --> 00:19:07.960
[USOPP] There's no way anybody was gonna
believe what I had to say. Why should they?

341
00:19:07.960 --> 00:19:10.800
Because what you were telling
them was the honest truth.

342
00:19:11.300 --> 00:19:14.340
They are coming. And they're
gonna level this whole town.

343
00:19:14.340 --> 00:19:16.890
Yeah, but what
am I supposed to do?

344
00:19:16.890 --> 00:19:19.390
They'll think I'm lying
if I try to warn them.

345
00:19:19.390 --> 00:19:23.930
Everyone in the village thinks that tomorrow's
just gonna be another normal day.

346
00:19:25.480 --> 00:19:27.520
They think I'm lying and that's
all they need to think.

347
00:19:27.520 --> 00:19:30.860
I'm gonna stop those pirates
at the beach tomorrow myself!

348
00:19:30.860 --> 00:19:34.820
This is all my fault
for being such a liar.

349
00:19:34.820 --> 00:19:40.660
I don't care anymore if they drive me
away with brooms or shoot me in the arm.

350
00:19:40.660 --> 00:19:42.490
This is my village.

351
00:19:42.490 --> 00:19:45.750
It's my home...
and I love everyone in it!

352
00:19:48.040 --> 00:19:50.670
I have to protect them.

353
00:19:51.630 --> 00:19:56.130
You're a hell of a good guy, sending
your cronies away and going into battle alone.

354
00:19:56.130 --> 00:19:59.640
[NAMI] Just so you know, I have dibs
on all the pirate treasure, you got it?

355
00:19:59.640 --> 00:20:01.890
So, you want
a little help or what?

356
00:20:01.890 --> 00:20:02.890
You guys...

357
00:20:02.890 --> 00:20:05.100
You're gonna help me fight
all these pirates?

358
00:20:05.100 --> 00:20:06.180
I don't get it?

359
00:20:06.180 --> 00:20:09.770
Well, you said there's
a whole buncha bad guys, right?

360
00:20:09.770 --> 00:20:11.770
And you look scared out
of your mind.

361
00:20:11.770 --> 00:20:14.320
Ugh. For your information,
I have nerves of steel!

362
00:20:14.320 --> 00:20:16.700
I'm perfectly okay
with tons of bad guys!

363
00:20:16.700 --> 00:20:19.610
After all, you're looking
at the legendary Captain Usopp,

364
00:20:19.610 --> 00:20:21.660
brave warrior of the high seas!

365
00:20:24.540 --> 00:20:27.500
Dammit! Alright,
fine, I'm scared!

366
00:20:27.500 --> 00:20:29.670
Why shouldn't I be?!
They're Captain Kuro's men!

367
00:20:29.670 --> 00:20:31.040
These guys mean business!

368
00:20:31.040 --> 00:20:32.540
I don't need pity!

369
00:20:32.540 --> 00:20:34.880
If you guys are sticking
around cause you pity me,

370
00:20:34.880 --> 00:20:37.170
just leave! I don't need
you laughin' at me!

371
00:20:37.170 --> 00:20:38.880
We're not laughing at you.

372
00:20:38.880 --> 00:20:42.140
We're helping
because you are honorable.

373
00:20:43.140 --> 00:20:46.100
You really think
we'd risk our lives out of pity?

374
00:20:53.110 --> 00:20:55.030
Aw... You guys!

375
00:21:08.210 --> 00:21:15.070
As a kid I had a dream of a dazzling treasure

376
00:21:15.270 --> 00:21:22.090
I had a map in my head that I knew would lead me

377
00:21:22.340 --> 00:21:29.190
Charted a course all on my own so nobody would beat me

378
00:21:29.310 --> 00:21:36.450
The promised land was in my hand drew a line in the sand

379
00:21:39.150 --> 00:21:41.830
Look where I am

380
00:21:44.060 --> 00:21:50.240
My one ambitions slipping right through my hands

381
00:21:50.580 --> 00:21:57.510
But if the world ever changes Ill call out your name

382
00:21:57.670 --> 00:22:04.590
We could return to a time when our lives were still the same

383
00:22:04.720 --> 00:22:11.720
Take me to the place where memories remain

384
00:22:11.820 --> 00:22:17.590
Please dont ever let them fade
